      "findings": [
        "DEP-015 FOUND AND REPAIRED: environment/Dockerfile carried --break-system-packages and a || pip install fallback on an official python:* base, which docker_generator.md forbids. Both were removed; the check now PASSES.",
        "CMP-019 FOUND AND REPAIRED: postgres and minio each carried restart: unless-stopped, which docker_generator.md forbids on a sidecar because a restart loop hides a boot failure. Both were removed; the check now PASSES.",
        "ARCH-002 / ARCH-003 NOT-APPLICABLE: no image is pinned by digest. Every image carries an explicit version tag, which resolves to a multi-architecture manifest list, so there is no digest to trace or to mis-select.",
        "DEP-016 / DEP-017 NOT-APPLICABLE: language is typescript, so there is no compiled-language build stage and no JRE to install.",
        "BP-004 NOT-APPLICABLE: no build-time download carries a source-provided checksum; the Node setup script and every package come from their official registries over TLS.",
        "ENV-002 NOT-APPLICABLE: the image ships no server, so there is no listening port for EXPOSE to match. The agent starts the app and the App Contract owns the port.",
        "BC-002 / BC-003 / BC-006 NOT-APPLICABLE: the image runs no application server. The bind address, the configured port and the production build are the agent's obligations and the brief states all three in the Deployment contract.",
        "CMP-020 NOT-APPLICABLE: superseded by CMP-022, which requires main to set extra_hosts and ports. A main that carried depends_on alone would lose every trial to the missing host-gateway mapping."
      ]
